# AI progress MD files

- While working on development tasks, AI agents should keep **temporary progress notes in Markdown** so work can resume after crashes, timeouts, or handoffs.
- Preferred location: **`.ai-progress/`** at the repo root (create as needed). Use short kebab-case names, e.g. `.ai-progress/hauling-db.md`, `.ai-progress/theme-pass.md`.
- These files are **local scratch only**:
  - Listed in `.gitignore` (`.ai-progress/` and similar).
  - **Must NOT be committed**, staged, or force-added.
  - Safe to overwrite; not a substitute for project-store docs or PR descriptions.
- When a task finishes cleanly, delete or leave the progress file — either is fine — but never ship it in git.
- Durable user-facing notes belong in Project store `docs/` or committed repo docs (`CONTRIBUTING.md`, etc.), not in `.ai-progress/`.
